            <ArticleTitle>Interleukin-18 is associated with protection against rhinovirus-induced colds and asthma exacerbations.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1528-31</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1093/cid/civ062</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Rhinoviruses cause the common cold and exacerbations of asthma. Animal models of infection have identified a protective role for interleukin-18 (IL-18). Following experimental rhinovirus infection, we observed increased respiratory symptoms in healthy and asthmatic subjects with low nasal and bronchial IL-18 levels.</AbstractText>
